{"jurisdiction":"NE","generatedAt":"2026-11-05T05:54:04Z","bills":{"NE-2025-LR384":{"id":"NE-2025-LR384","passed":false,"number":"LR 384","title":"Interim study to review the Licensing of Truth and Deception Examiners Act and any rules and regulations for truth and deception examiners in furtherance of the purposes of the Occupational Board Reform Act","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-20","sponsor":{"name":"Sanders","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"45"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-15","text":"Notice of hearing for November 05, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-08-14","text":"Notice of hearing for October 30, 2026 (cancel)","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-08-14","text":"Notice of hearing for October 30, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-30","text":"Referred to Government, Military and Veterans Affairs Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-20","text":"Referred to Executive Board","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-20","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2026","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR384.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR384.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The resolution would direct a legislative committee to study the rules for licensing truth and deception examiners in Nebraska. The review would look at whether the current rules best protect the public while also preserving the right to work in a lawful job and supporting more competition and new ideas. After the study, the committee would report its findings and recommendations to the Legislature or the Legislative Council.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"NE-2025-LR433":{"id":"NE-2025-LR433","passed":false,"number":"LR 433","title":"Interim study to examine the necessity of a robust and well-integrated education and workforce system to support long-term economic growth that enables learners to move efficiently from education and training to employment in high-demand and high-wage occupations across the state","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-24","sponsor":{"name":"Dover","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"19"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-09-09","text":"Notice of hearing for October 30, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-08-28","text":"Notice of hearing for October 23, 2026 (cancel)","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-08-14","text":"Notice of hearing for October 23, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-30","text":"Referred to Education Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-24","text":"Referred to Executive Board","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-24","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2026","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR433.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR433.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The resolution would direct the Legislature’s Education Committee to study how Nebraska can better connect education, training, and jobs for workers in high-demand, high-wage fields. The study would look at data systems, the Nebraska Statewide Workforce and Educational Reporting System, ways to link education and job data, and possible changes to rules on sharing data while protecting privacy. The committee would report its findings and recommendations after the study.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"NE-2025-LR419":{"id":"NE-2025-LR419","passed":false,"number":"LR 419","title":"Interim study to examine volunteer burnout on municipal boards and commissions and identify specific municipal boards or commissions that could effectively function with a reduced number of members","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-24","sponsor":{"name":"Urban Affairs Committee","party":null,"state":"NE","district":null},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-09-03","text":"Notice of hearing for November 06, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-30","text":"Referred to Urban Affairs Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-24","text":"Referred to Executive Board","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-24","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2026","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR419.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR419.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"This resolution would call for an interim study, which is a study done between sessions, on volunteer burnout on city boards and commissions. It would also look for specific local boards or commissions that could work with fewer members.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"NE-2025-LR391":{"id":"NE-2025-LR391","passed":false,"number":"LR 391","title":"Interim study to examine the issue of diaper access for Nebraska families","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-20","sponsor":{"name":"Dungan","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"26"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-07-21","text":"Notice of hearing for September 17, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-30","text":"Referred to Health and Human Services Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-20","text":"Referred to Executive Board","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-20","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2026","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR391.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR391.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"This resolution would direct the Health and Human Services Committee to study diaper access for Nebraska families. The study would look at how diaper need affects children, mothers, health care, public health, work, and child care, as well as what resources exist in the state and how other states handle it. The committee would then report its findings and recommendations to the Legislature or Legislative Council.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"NE-2025-LR475":{"id":"NE-2025-LR475","passed":false,"number":"LR 475","title":"Interim study to conduct a comprehensive review of state funding provided to nonprofit organizations","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-25","sponsor":{"name":"Andersen","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"49"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-07-08","text":"Notice of hearing for October 09, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-30","text":"Referred to Appropriations Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-25","text":"Referred to Executive Board","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-25","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2026","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR475.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR475.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The resolution would order an interim study of state money given to nonprofit groups, especially groups that are tax-free under federal law. The study would look at who gets the money, where it comes from, how much is given, what it can be used for, and how well it is tracked. The Appropriations Committee would do the study and then report its findings and recommendations to lawmakers.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"NE-2025-LR33":{"id":"NE-2025-LR33","passed":false,"number":"LR 33","title":"Recommend that the Nebraska Congressional delegation take affirmative action to reform the present approach to daylight saving time","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2025-01-29","sponsor":{"name":"Conrad","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"46"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-04-17","text":"Indefinitely postponed","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-01-07","text":"Title printed. Carryover resolution","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2025-03-10","text":"Notice of hearing for March 20, 2025","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2025-01-30","text":"Referred to Government, Military and Veterans Affairs Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2025-01-29","text":"Referred to Reference Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2025-01-29","text":"Laid over","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2025-01-29","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2025","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR33.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR33.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[{"label":"Statement of Intent","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/SI/LR33.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"This resolution would ask Nebraska’s members of Congress to take action to change how daylight saving time is handled. It says the change should aim to improve health, business output, farm work, public safety, and keep time rules the same across the country. It would also send copies of the resolution to federal leaders and Nebraska’s congressional delegation.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"NE-2025-LB795":{"id":"NE-2025-LB795","passed":true,"number":"LB 795","title":"Designate bromazolam as a controlled substance under the Uniform Controlled Substances Act, correct the spelling of certain controlled substances, and enhance penalties for certain controlled substance offenses involving fentanyl","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-01-07","sponsor":{"name":"DeKay","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"40"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-04-17","text":"Provisions/portions of LB817 amended into LB795 by AM2092","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-03","text":"Approved by Governor on March 3, 2026","chamber":"Governor"},{"date":"2026-03-03","text":"Presented to Governor on February 27, 2026","chamber":"Governor"},{"date":"2026-02-27","text":"President/Speaker signed","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-02-27","text":"Passed on Final Reading 32-14-3","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-02-